@@ -23,4 +23,20 @@ Resolve the immutable source revision before rendering. The cache key includes c
 
 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+The worker implements 2Q eviction. In-memory metadata tracks two private FIFO queues, Q1 for first-use entries and Q2 for entries reused after an initial access. On a cache hit, an entry moves from Q1 to Q2 on its second access; entries already in Q2 are promoted to the front of Q2. On a cache miss that results in admission, the entry is placed in Q1. Eviction prefers Q1, removing from its tail, to protect reused comparison sheets from one-off screening scans. Q1 and Q2 share the 12 GiB budget with a configurable size split; the split is tunable at startup and is recorded as an operational parameter. All replacement bookkeeping remains private to the preview worker.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Eviction policy | 2Q with two private FIFO queues and configurable Q1/Q2 size split | LRU; frequency-based eviction with aging | Protects repeatedly accessed comparison sheets from eviction by one-off sequential screenings. Extra bookkeeping is acceptable per project tenet to keep replacement private to the worker. LRU is vulnerable to scans; frequency with aging adds counter maintenance and lags project switches. |
+| Cache key | clip ID + revision + renderer version | clip ID only; clip ID + revision | Matches HLD tenet to key by immutable revision and renderer version, ensuring correctness across re-renders. |
+
+## Open Questions & Future Decisions
+
+### Resolved
+1. ✅ Eviction policy selected as 2Q per user decision 2026-10-16.
+
+### Deferred
+1. Exact Q1/Q2 size split value to tune during pilot.
+2. Whether to cap Q2 growth to preserve headroom for new screening waves.
